WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.752
Merci for the shower.

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.128
-La douche.
-What?

00:00:03.212 --> 00:00:05.172
The shower is la douche.

00:00:05.255 --> 00:00:06.256
Oh.

00:00:06.757 --> 00:00:07.716
Well,

00:00:07.799 --> 00:00:09.510
I had a wonderful

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:10.844
douche.

00:00:12.804 --> 00:00:14.848
Ugh, this can't
be happening. Come on!

00:00:18.977 --> 00:00:20.229
Sorry, I...

00:00:20.312 --> 00:00:23.524
I thought this was
my apartment. Fifth floor?

00:00:23.607 --> 00:00:25.275
This is the fourth floor.

00:00:26.527 --> 00:00:27.361
Fifth floor.

00:00:28.362 --> 00:00:29.196
Right.

00:00:39.122 --> 00:00:40.374
Oh, jeez.

00:00:40.958 --> 00:00:43.252
I did it again.
I'm really so sorry.

00:00:43.335 --> 00:00:45.671
Emily, do you want
to live in my apartment?

00:00:45.754 --> 00:00:47.422
Come on, I mean,
even you have to admit

00:00:47.506 --> 00:00:49.550
that the floor number here
makes absolutely no sense.

00:00:49.633 --> 00:00:51.134
I have to get to work,

00:00:51.218 --> 00:00:54.096
but, um, I promise I won't
bang on your door again.

00:00:54.179 --> 00:00:55.013
No problem.

00:00:55.681 --> 00:00:56.807
Bang anytime.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.934
No, here,
the customer is never right.

00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:01.144
Maybe I'll educate
the chef a little bit

00:01:01.228 --> 00:01:02.688
about customer service.

00:01:02.771 --> 00:01:03.897
You think
you're gonna change

00:01:03.981 --> 00:01:05.148
the entire French culture

00:01:05.232 --> 00:01:06.316
by sending back a steak?

00:01:08.861 --> 00:01:09.695
Gabriel!

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:11.154
Emily.

00:01:14.366 --> 00:01:15.534
Hi, can you come talk
to my plumber?

00:01:15.617 --> 00:01:16.618
It's an emergency.

00:01:16.702 --> 00:01:18.954
Good morning, Gabriel.
How are you today?

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.206
Good morning, Gabriel.
How are you today?

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:22.708
Asleep.
Thank you for asking.

00:01:22.791 --> 00:01:24.459
I was having
a very nice dream,

00:01:24.543 --> 00:01:25.669
and this American girl

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:27.337
banged on my door
and woke me up.

00:01:28.213 --> 00:01:29.214
Or maybe I'm still dreaming?

00:01:29.298 --> 00:01:31.049
Uh, you're not still
dreaming. You're wide awake.

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:32.968
Don't let him leave
until he fixes my shower.

00:01:33.552 --> 00:01:36.180
He lives downstairs. I don't
want to make it complicated.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:38.473
Oh, sometimes
the best relationships

00:01:38.557 --> 00:01:39.641
are complicated.

00:01:42.644 --> 00:01:43.770
Did you forget something?

00:01:44.521 --> 00:01:45.355
I did.

00:01:49.276 --> 00:01:50.444
Do you guys know each other?

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:53.280
Turns out we do.

00:01:53.363 --> 00:01:54.948
See? I told you.

00:01:55.032 --> 00:01:56.491
Paris seems like a big city,

00:01:56.575 --> 00:01:58.285
but it's really
just a small town.

00:01:59.286 --> 00:02:00.829
I'm so happy to see you!

00:02:02.372 --> 00:02:04.458
I really wish Gabriel had
told me he had a girlfriend

00:02:04.541 --> 00:02:05.709
before I thanked him
with my mouth.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.169
I thought
you just kissed him?

00:02:07.252 --> 00:02:08.086
I did.

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:10.797
Your English is as confusing
as your French.

00:02:10.881 --> 00:02:13.050
Yeah, I feel stupid.
In both languages.

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:14.551
I really like her.

00:02:15.052 --> 00:02:16.094
She likes you, too.

00:02:16.845 --> 00:02:17.888
I wouldn't have kissed you

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:19.473
if I knew
you had a girlfriend.

00:02:19.556 --> 00:02:20.516
It's okay. You didn't know.

00:02:20.599 --> 00:02:22.059
Why didn't you tell me?

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:23.977
I didn't know
you were going to kiss me.

00:02:24.061 --> 00:02:25.521
Well, I just thought
that you felt...

00:02:26.939 --> 00:02:29.024
Ugh!
Doesn't matter now, so...

00:02:29.691 --> 00:02:31.401
Clearly, it was just me,

00:02:31.485 --> 00:02:34.404
and I made it all up
in my head, so...

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:35.989
Forget it.

00:02:36.073 --> 00:02:37.115
Forget what?

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.576
The kiss in your kitchen.

00:02:40.661 --> 00:02:41.787
I don't remember.

00:02:42.704 --> 00:02:44.581
It must not
have been very good.

00:02:44.665 --> 00:02:45.874
It wasn't just you.

00:02:53.674 --> 00:02:54.800
I felt it, too.

00:02:59.513 --> 00:03:00.472
Good night, Gabriel.

00:03:05.894 --> 00:03:06.937
Emily, hi.

00:03:07.896 --> 00:03:09.314
Where are you off to
so dressed up?

00:03:09.398 --> 00:03:11.567
Oh, I have tickets
to the ballet.

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:14.111
Oh, with Thomas, I presume?

00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:15.487
Do you have
a problem with him?

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:19.032
I'm sorry,
but I think he's a snob.

00:03:19.616 --> 00:03:22.035
An asshole masquerading
as an intellectual.

00:03:22.119 --> 00:03:23.495
I know his type.

00:03:23.579 --> 00:03:24.621
Maybe...

00:03:24.705 --> 00:03:26.540
Maybe you can't tell
since you're not from Paris.

00:03:26.623 --> 00:03:27.958
Well, you're not
from Paris, either.

00:03:29.835 --> 00:03:30.961
Sorry, I...

00:03:31.753 --> 00:03:33.422
-It's not how I meant it.
-Fine.

00:03:33.505 --> 00:03:35.174
I just think
you're wasting your time

00:03:35.257 --> 00:03:36.842
on a guy
who doesn't deserve you.

00:03:36.925 --> 00:03:38.093
Okay, just one fun drink,

00:03:38.177 --> 00:03:39.344
and then we have
to get out of here.

00:03:40.679 --> 00:03:41.513
Just one?

00:03:42.723 --> 00:03:44.183
She's fun.

00:03:44.266 --> 00:03:45.726
She's not supposed
to be that fun.

00:03:45.809 --> 00:03:48.937
She's voicing Mother Goose
in a Pixar movie.

00:03:49.021 --> 00:03:49.855
Well, it's a good thing

00:03:49.938 --> 00:03:51.190
no one's
paying attention here.

00:03:51.273 --> 00:03:53.859
Yeah, at home,
she's the good girl,

00:03:53.942 --> 00:03:55.027
but here--

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:56.904
She can get away
with everything.

00:03:56.987 --> 00:03:57.821
It's just Paris.

00:03:57.905 --> 00:03:59.239
It's not some
alternate universe

00:03:59.323 --> 00:04:00.991
where rules don't apply.

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:03.660
We don't come to Paris
to be good.

00:04:17.174 --> 00:04:18.008
Uh...

00:04:20.552 --> 00:04:21.470
Um...

00:04:22.429 --> 00:04:25.557
I'm not somebody
who can share a crêpe.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:28.185
-I need the whole crêpe.
-Emily--

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:30.395
I don't think we should
see each other anymore.

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:33.607
It's not good for any of us.

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:35.609
I was just offering you
a ride home.

00:04:36.193 --> 00:04:37.402
A sunrise...

00:04:40.322 --> 00:04:42.574
Thank you again
for your help.

00:04:43.909 --> 00:04:45.202
I can get myself home.

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:48.580
Emily, have you tasted
this man's coq au vin?

00:04:49.081 --> 00:04:50.374
I definitely have not.

00:04:50.457 --> 00:04:52.543
I tell you,
when it hit my lips,

00:04:52.626 --> 00:04:54.670
I was ready
to propose to him.

00:04:54.753 --> 00:04:56.004
I feel like
we've made it pretty clear

00:04:56.088 --> 00:04:57.214
that we can't
just be friends.

00:04:57.297 --> 00:04:58.465
But we live
on top of each other.

00:04:58.549 --> 00:04:59.800
You're proving my point.

00:04:59.883 --> 00:05:01.134
So what?
We just stop speaking?

00:05:01.218 --> 00:05:02.135
What do we tell Camille?

00:05:02.219 --> 00:05:03.804
We don't
tell Camille anything.

00:05:03.887 --> 00:05:04.847
We just have to be friendly.

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:06.348
-But not friends?
-Yes.

00:05:06.431 --> 00:05:07.683
Can you make me
a list of rules?

00:05:07.766 --> 00:05:08.892
Because
it's a little complicated.

00:05:08.976 --> 00:05:10.561
Okay, fine.
I'll make it easy.

00:05:10.644 --> 00:05:11.854
You go to the market,

00:05:11.937 --> 00:05:12.855
I'll go on the tour,

00:05:12.938 --> 00:05:14.606
and everybody keeps
their hands to themselves.

00:05:16.733 --> 00:05:17.609
Hmm...

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:20.195
Wow, this…
this chicken is...

00:05:20.279 --> 00:05:22.030
I told you.

00:05:22.114 --> 00:05:23.198
His coq is the best.

00:05:23.907 --> 00:05:28.036
-It… it really is delicious.
-Hmm, and so juicy.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:30.414
Well, since you didn't
get to try my eggplant,

00:05:30.497 --> 00:05:32.332
at least
you're enjoying my coq.

00:05:32.416 --> 00:05:34.209
Gabriel found a restaurant
he can afford.

00:05:34.793 --> 00:05:35.794
Isn't that good news?

00:05:35.878 --> 00:05:38.005
The restaurant
isn't in Paris, Emily.

00:05:38.088 --> 00:05:39.256
It's in Normandy,
where he's from.

00:05:39.339 --> 00:05:40.716
What? He…?

00:05:41.425 --> 00:05:42.467
He's moving to Normandy?

00:05:42.551 --> 00:05:43.760
You and Camille?

00:05:45.804 --> 00:05:47.181
We want different things
right now,

00:05:47.264 --> 00:05:48.265
and...

00:05:49.183 --> 00:05:50.475
we need to be free
to do them.

00:05:51.226 --> 00:05:52.060
What does that mean?

00:05:53.145 --> 00:05:54.771
Well, she's not coming
to Normandy,

00:05:54.855 --> 00:05:55.981
and I'm not staying
in Paris,

00:05:56.064 --> 00:05:59.985
so we will just go
our own ways.

00:06:00.986 --> 00:06:01.945
Gabriel!

00:06:02.029 --> 00:06:03.113
Hello?

00:06:04.865 --> 00:06:06.158
Gabriel!

00:06:11.955 --> 00:06:12.831
Emily?

00:06:16.293 --> 00:06:17.294
I...

00:06:17.377 --> 00:06:18.670
I just… I...

00:06:18.754 --> 00:06:20.255
I didn't want that
to be the last time

00:06:20.339 --> 00:06:21.798
that we saw each other,
and I'm...

00:06:21.882 --> 00:06:23.217
I'm gonna miss you so much!

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:24.343
And I...

00:06:37.648 --> 00:06:39.733
You said
that you were leaving.

00:06:39.816 --> 00:06:41.777
Tell me you didn't feel
everything that I felt.

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:44.029
I can't do this to Camille.

00:06:44.112 --> 00:06:45.614
I don't want
to hurt Camille, either.

00:06:45.697 --> 00:06:47.908
I… But I can't stop
thinking about you.

00:06:49.368 --> 00:06:50.536
About us...

00:06:50.619 --> 00:06:52.871
I'm still in love
with Gabriel, Emily.

00:06:53.914 --> 00:06:55.499
And I'm afraid
I've lost him.

00:06:57.209 --> 00:06:58.210
You haven't.

00:06:58.293 --> 00:06:59.962
This is just
such a huge mess.

00:07:00.045 --> 00:07:00.879
I know.

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:02.673
And I'm sorry.

00:07:03.173 --> 00:07:04.007
I really am.

00:07:04.091 --> 00:07:06.635
You know, leek is not
an American vegetable

00:07:06.718 --> 00:07:08.554
that hits you
over the head with flavour.

00:07:08.637 --> 00:07:10.013
It's subtle.

00:07:10.097 --> 00:07:11.390
Elusive.

00:07:12.558 --> 00:07:14.142
It's so misunderstood.

00:07:15.644 --> 00:07:16.895
What?

00:07:16.979 --> 00:07:17.938
Don't laugh at the leek.

00:07:19.022 --> 00:07:20.482
Okay, let me show you.

00:07:20.566 --> 00:07:22.901
Oh, no, no, no.
You have to cut that bit.

00:07:22.985 --> 00:07:24.278
I… I look ridiculous
in this one.

00:07:24.361 --> 00:07:25.863
-No, I think you look great.
-Come on.

00:07:25.946 --> 00:07:27.656
-It was candid.
-No, no, no. Please, please!

00:07:27.739 --> 00:07:28.907
-No.
-Please, delete it. Please.

00:07:28.991 --> 00:07:31.702
No, it's my account.
You have to trust me.

00:07:31.785 --> 00:07:33.620
-It's my face.
-You have to trust me.

00:07:39.042 --> 00:07:39.960
So...

00:07:41.170 --> 00:07:43.130
did you get
everything you want?

00:07:49.386 --> 00:07:51.138
I'm only in Paris
for a year.

00:07:51.221 --> 00:07:52.556
It's always been the deal.

00:07:52.639 --> 00:07:55.642
And I don't want us
to start something

00:07:56.435 --> 00:07:57.436
that we can't continue.

00:07:57.519 --> 00:08:00.439
This you and me…
It's a… It's a fantasy.

00:08:00.522 --> 00:08:01.398
It's a...

00:08:01.899 --> 00:08:03.984
-A Paris fantasy.
-Hey, hey, hey.

00:08:05.068 --> 00:08:06.653
It's not a fantasy to me.

00:08:06.737 --> 00:08:09.114
We both know that you're
not moving to Chicago,

00:08:09.198 --> 00:08:10.574
and I'm not
staying in Paris.

00:08:11.867 --> 00:08:13.452
Then what?

00:08:13.535 --> 00:08:16.121
And I'm not going
to fall in love with you

00:08:16.205 --> 00:08:18.123
when we have
an expiration date.

00:08:18.749 --> 00:08:20.542
You don't text me back
or answer my calls,

00:08:20.626 --> 00:08:22.169
and then
you just show up here?

00:08:23.003 --> 00:08:24.087
What?

00:08:24.171 --> 00:08:25.839
Em, I lost my phone.

00:08:25.923 --> 00:08:27.382
I had no way
of contacting you.

00:08:27.466 --> 00:08:28.967
I couldn't remember
where you worked.

00:08:29.051 --> 00:08:30.969
But I remembered you
did an event at this place.

00:08:31.637 --> 00:08:32.763
I'm pretty sure

00:08:32.846 --> 00:08:35.182
it's in that suit jacket
of mine you stole.

00:08:37.267 --> 00:08:38.185
Oh.

00:08:40.062 --> 00:08:40.979
That jacket.

00:08:41.063 --> 00:08:42.356
He's the reason.

00:08:44.858 --> 00:08:46.610
Yeah, I guess.

00:08:46.693 --> 00:08:47.861
He's the reason.

00:08:47.945 --> 00:08:49.321
Well, it's good
to know the truth...

00:08:50.155 --> 00:08:51.448
even if it's hard to watch.

00:08:51.532 --> 00:08:53.325
Do you think
you could spare us a table?

00:08:54.159 --> 00:08:55.619
It would be my pleasure.

00:08:55.702 --> 00:08:58.372
I think I understand your
type a little better now.

00:08:58.455 --> 00:09:00.332
English, less complicated...

00:09:00.415 --> 00:09:02.960
Yeah, way less complicated.

00:09:03.043 --> 00:09:05.254
He doesn't have a girlfriend
I'm also friends with.

00:09:05.921 --> 00:09:07.256
It's over.
We're just friends.

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:09.550
And as her friend...

00:09:11.593 --> 00:09:13.178
I'm glad
she's with a good guy.

00:09:13.679 --> 00:09:16.431
Okay, you need to decide
what you want

00:09:16.515 --> 00:09:18.392
and not what's going
to make everyone else happy.

00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:22.980
This isn't just
a fun year abroad anymore.

00:09:23.772 --> 00:09:25.190
This is your life.

00:09:27.109 --> 00:09:29.862
I think I'm staying in Paris
for longer than a year.

00:09:30.988 --> 00:09:32.322
Oh. For how long?

00:09:32.406 --> 00:09:34.741
I don't know.
Indefinitely. Maybe.

00:09:35.534 --> 00:09:37.369
When I came here, Paris
was this fun little detour

00:09:37.452 --> 00:09:39.246
that I thought
would be a good story,

00:09:39.329 --> 00:09:41.373
but now I think this detour
is where I'm supposed to be,

00:09:41.456 --> 00:09:42.833
because my life is here now,
you know.

00:09:42.916 --> 00:09:44.710
My friends, my career and...

00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:46.295
you.

00:09:46.378 --> 00:09:47.588
Emily, I should tell you--

00:09:47.671 --> 00:09:48.964
And I just need
to say this, okay,

00:09:49.047 --> 00:09:50.424
before I lose the nerve.

00:09:50.507 --> 00:09:52.551
I just need to tell you
that the reason

00:09:52.634 --> 00:09:54.511
I said I couldn't
be with you, okay,

00:09:54.595 --> 00:09:55.804
wasn't Alfie.

00:09:56.305 --> 00:09:57.181
Gabriel, I'm--

00:09:57.264 --> 00:10:00.058
I made some room,

00:10:01.518 --> 00:10:03.103
but I think we're gonna
need another dresser.

00:10:03.937 --> 00:10:04.771
Emily.

00:10:05.522 --> 00:10:06.565
Hi.

00:10:08.817 --> 00:10:10.611
Gabriel asked me to move in.

00:10:15.115 --> 00:10:15.949
Oh, wow!

00:10:17.534 --> 00:10:19.119
You guys are back together.

00:10:19.703 --> 00:10:23.248
Yeah, we wanted to tell you,
but it just happened, so...

00:10:25.751 --> 00:10:26.960
That's great.

00:10:27.586 --> 00:10:28.504
That's great.

00:10:28.587 --> 00:10:30.422
Yay! Neighbours!

00:10:31.757 --> 00:10:33.926
Well, I guess I'll just
see you around, then.

